        "summary": "- Main purpose: a hub/catalog for Automation & AI testing courses and interactive demo pages (practice modules) hosted by WebDriver University.\n- Main user flows: browse/select course or demo tiles via navigation/toggle, open interactive modules (e.g., BUTTON CLICKS, TO DO LIST, IFRAME, FILE UPLOAD, DATEPICKER), use CONTACT US form, and use LOGIN PORTAL.\n- Key interactive targets: demo pages with IDs (#button-clicks, #to-do-list, #iframe, #file-upload, #ajax-loader, #datepicker, #hidden-elements, #popup-alerts, #dropdown-checkboxes-radiobuttons, etc.).\n- Typical actions: click/toggle nav items, submit login/contact forms, upload files, pick dates, interact with alerts/iframes, wait for AJAX, scroll and perform action sequences.\n- Important edge cases: asynchronous loads and timing (AJAX loader, delayed elements), iframe cross-origin and focus/selector scope, hidden/disabled elements and reveal behaviors, file upload size/type errors, datepicker bounds/formatting, modal/alert interrupting flows, stale element references after DOM updates.\n- Other considerations: navigation toggle responsiveness, stateful flows (session/login persistence), accessibility and keyboard interactions for interactive widgets.",
